      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. so basically, even if someone thinks they are moderating for \"safety\" or \"truth,\" it's fundamentally a bad idea because the state isn't actually any more reliable than the users. do you think the common counter-argument—that we need regulation to prevent actual harm or fake news—is actually a valid concern, or is it just an excuse for censorship?",
